    "summary": "The theme root is the body in every shell, so the light or dark mode reaches the whole document and the body background paints the canvas (the root has min-height 100vh and 56px top padding). Pages open in light unless a mode was stored; the OS colour-scheme preference is no longer consulted in either script. The font-face rules sit in a style element instead of showing as text. The theme switch is a fixed 32px top-right button, a direct child of the body, in the companion, docgen and fallback pages. The companion header stacks and its table shrinks at 480px and below. A live headless Chrome test (INSRC_LIVE_TESTS=1) checks the companion page at 1280px and 360px and the docgen page; screenshots are under S001/screenshots. Left out: the companion .vp-bar toolbar is still not styled by the shared .iv-bar rules (existing).",
